# Playwright's per-run report and screenshots, written on a failing spec.
test-results/

# Half-finished extractions from the module split. `check.sh` globs `src/*.js` and
# `wired.mjs` is handed the same list, so a file with any other extension sits in
# the module folder and is read by no gate at all - which is how a one-line
# `src/graphics.js.deferred` spent three commits in the tree.
*.deferred
*.bak
*.orig

# The prop library and its maps are build artefacts: `meshes/*.glb` and
# `meshes/tex/*.png` are 77 MB written by the pages in `meshes/build-*.html` and by
# the dev server's `/__save` hook. **Everything in `meshes/` that is not one of
# those is source** - the two modules every builder page imports, and the four
# builder pages themselves, which are the only way to regenerate the artefacts -
# so the ignore is a deny with exceptions rather than a deny of the folder. A
# clone with these in it can build the county; a clone without them cannot build
# the game, cannot run `tools/check.sh`, and cannot run `tools/wired.mjs` at all,
# since it is handed both modules by name.
/meshes/*
!/meshes/palette.js
!/meshes/maps.js
!/meshes/build-*.html

# `.kilo/` holds the session's plans and skills, and `references/` whatever was
# read in to write them. Neither is the game.
.kilo/
references/